      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Worktree from origin/master. Map E11's inputs, and what the invite flow writes to a contact.</step>
    <step>Rule (1), with the intent fact added to the decision input and a fail-closed read.</step>
    <step>Rule (2), the ObjectConflict branch with its email and outcome.</step>
    <step>Tests, mutation proofs, build, ArchTests, and the ExternalAccess, binding and invite unit tests. Open the PR into master.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>No existing record distinguishes an invited contact from an uninvited one: STOP, report what exists, and propose the narrowest option.</trigger>
    <trigger>The rule would change a workforce-plane outcome that a 141 test pins: STOP and report it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>CIAM plane, unbound contact with a matching email and an active grant here: binds (BindByEmail).</criterion>
    <criterion>CIAM plane, unbound contact with a matching email and a pending invite here: binds.</criterion>
    <criterion>CIAM plane, unbound contact with a matching email, no active grant and no pending invite: denied with the new deny code, and nothing written.</criterion>
    <criterion>The grant is expired or deactivated, and there is no invite: denied.</criterion>
    <criterion>The intent read faults: never binds (deny or 503, per the existing mapping).</criterion>
    <criterion>Workforce-plane E11 outcomes are unchanged, and the 141 tests are unchanged and green.</criterion>
    <criterion>Invite of an email whose CIAM account exists (Graph 400 ObjectConflict): the invite succeeds with outcome ExistingAccount, the contact stays pending, the sign-in email is sent, and no onboarding email is sent.</criterion>
    <criterion>Any other Graph 400 or 5xx: today's failure path, unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion>Mutation proofs: removing the intent gate, treating a fault as intent, and treating every 400 as ExistingAccount each fail their test.</criterion>
    <criterion>The BFF builds with 0 errors. Spaarke.ArchTests all pass, including RouteAuthorizationGuard and the census. The PR targets master.</criterion>
    <criterion>Test scope: the cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
